PROBLEM="Build a LINQ transform whose result can be read multiple times without re-running the source or causing multiple enumeration."
LEARNINGS="LINQ (Where/Select) is DEFERRED: the query does not run until enumerated, and it re-runs on EACH enumeration. If the result is read more than once (or the source has side effects / is expensive / single-shot), MATERIALIZE once with ToList()/ToArray() and return IReadOnlyList<T>. This guarantees the source is enumerated exactly once and reads are stable."
ERRORS="Do NOT return the raw IEnumerable from a Where/Select chain when it will be enumerated multiple times - that re-executes the whole pipeline each time (multiple enumeration), re-hitting the source/DB and breaking single-shot sequences."
TAGS="src:context7 lang:csharp area:linq"
REF_SRC="Pipe.cs"
